From f63c16cf5035f24b05261c757aaef949bb91fdbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:36:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] cron: a requested stop (cancel, Stop, remove) logs a
 WARNING, not 'Job failed' (cron-7c04faf754)

remove_job / hermes cron cancel / Desktop Stop write the execution's cancel
marker; the run's stop check raised a plain RuntimeError for anything but
this gateway's shutdown, so run_job logged ERROR 'Job ... failed:' with a
traceback and the coach filed a self-heal defect for a deliberate stop.

_abort_if_fire_claim_lost now raises CronRunCancelled when the marker exists
(whichever latch fired first: remove_job also drops the claim) and names the
marker's reason; _log_shutdown_stop -> _log_expected_stop logs one WARNING
'Job <name> stopped on request: ...'. A claim lost with no marker stays a
RuntimeError logged at ERROR with its traceback.

Regression: tests/cron/test_requested_stop_logging.py (red on 5ecbb476e20).
---
